STATEMENT OF DERIVATION

This software is a derivative work of Health-GPS, the population health
microsimulation developed by the Centre for Health Economics & Policy Innovation
at Imperial College London and INRAE, France, and distributed under the BSD
3-Clause License reproduced above.

It is a new implementation rather than a fork: the code here was written for this
repository, but its behaviour, its data formats, its configuration format and its
test suite derive directly from that work, and parts of it were ported from
Health-GPS source. Files that derive from Health-GPS source carry a header saying
so. The copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer above are retained as clauses
1 and 2 of that licence require.

Neither the names of the copyright holders above nor those of their contributors
are used to endorse or promote this derived work, and no endorsement by them is
implied or should be inferred (clause 3).

Where this implementation intentionally behaves differently from Health-GPS, the
difference is recorded in docs/deviations.md with the evidence for it.

The Health-GPS *data* — the UN World Population Prospects demographic series and
the IHME disease series — is NOT part of this repository and is not covered by
this licence. It carries its own, more restrictive terms, the IHME data under
CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. This repository fetches that data on demand and vendors none of
it; see docs/decisions/0011-data-fetched-not-vendored.md. The synthetic data pack
under tests/fixtures/ contains invented numbers only and is covered by this
licence.
